Z||000000||baggy||01-23-2000||07:04 PM||||hello, my name is Chris, I live in B'ham Alabama, I'm 35 and divorced..nuff said..<BR>I recently got this 1984 SE 2m4 4-speed from my dad, who horsetraded for it and decided he felt uncomfortable driving it..(to low, to squirrly, to RED..LOL)<BR>anyways, it's my first Fiero,<BR>the first time i've rode in one<BR>the first time I've owned one..<BR>and the first time I've worked on one...<BR>as evidenced by the burn marks on my forearm...<BR>I've never felt this way about a car..<BR>even if it's only got a four banger,and a chevette(I just found this out) front end..<BR>I know where to pick up a couple of junkers so parts wont be a problem.<BR>so far the car is still stock pwr windows, pwr locks am-fm cassettte.<BR>the speakers in the seats even work real good..<BR>any tips on how to upgrade those would be helpfull..<BR>the only thing I changed was the stock four by tens..<BR>I toook the factory 10ohm speakers out and replaces tem with 8ohm speakers from Radio Shack..<BR>costs 10.00 each..<BR>good sound upgrade..<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||01-23-2000||07:11 PM||||Welcome baggy, to the best bunch of Fieroholics in the world! Pick up one of those parts cars when you get the chance, mines been a big help and learning experience as well!||||reg||14
Z||000002||Carrolles||01-24-2000||07:02 AM||||Baggy,<BR>Welcome to the Forum.  I'm in Alabaster with a silver 85SE 2m6 4speed.<BR>Dave Hunter is the president of Alabama Fieros and lives in B'hm also although most of the members live in the Huntsville area.<BR>Plan to visit Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory someday in Toney (north of Huntsville a few miles).  There will be a swap meet there at the end of April.<BR>Take a look here: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/al2/alabamafieros/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/al2/alabamafieros/index.html</A> <P>Looking forward to meeting you someday.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
